hyprmoncfg is a terminal-first monitor configurator and auto-switching
daemon for Hyprland.

It provides a text UI for arranging monitors spatially, saving monitor
profiles, and restoring the best matching profile when displays are added
or removed.

This SlackBuild uses the upstream source tarball and a pre-fetched Go
module cache tarball from the matching GitHub release so the build does not
download Go modules during compilation.
